**Requirements.** N x N board (default 3), two players alternate, win with a full row, column or diagonal, detect draw, reject invalid moves. Extensions: undo, multiple games, spectators, hints.

**Entities.** `Game` (id, board, players, currentPlayer, status, winner), `Board` (size and counters), `Player`, `Move` (player, row, col), `GameStatus` (IN_PROGRESS, WON, DRAW). `GameService` exposes `createGame`, `makeMove`, `getGame`.

**Move API.** `makeMove(gameId, playerId, row, col)` returns `{status, board, winner?, nextPlayer}` or an error. Validation: game exists and is in progress, it is the caller's turn, the cell is in range and empty.

**O(1) win check.** Keep `rows[N]`, `cols[N]`, `diag`, `antiDiag` counters. For player `p` (+1 or -1), after a move at (r, c): `rows[r] += p; cols[c] += p;` if `r == c` then `diag += p`; if `r + c == N-1` then `antiDiag += p`. If any equals `N` in absolute value, that player has won. A draw is reached when `moves == N*N` with no winner. Memory is O(N) and each move is O(1), compared with rescanning the board in O(N^2).

```java
int p = player == X ? 1 : -1;
rows[r] += p; cols[c] += p;
if (r == c) diag += p;
if (r + c == n - 1) anti += p;
if (Math.abs(rows[r]) == n || Math.abs(cols[c]) == n
    || Math.abs(diag) == n || Math.abs(anti) == n) status = WON;
```

**Scalability.** Make `GameService` stateless and store game state in Redis or a database, keyed by game id. Protect against concurrent moves with optimistic locking (version number) or a per-game lock. Use WebSockets for live updates. Shard by game id.

**AI hints.** Add a `HintService` behind an interface (Strategy). For tic-tac-toe, minimax with alpha-beta pruning is exact and cheap; for larger boards or natural-language explanations, call a model. Call it asynchronously with a timeout and rate limit, cache by board state, and fall back to a heuristic (win now, block, centre). Never let the hint service change game state.
